Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-07
Subject: Make TElf32ObjectData.Create an explicit override
License: expat

TAsmObjectData.Create(const n:string) is virtual.  TElf32ObjectData.Create
has the same signature but is not declared "override".  FPC treats that as a
reintroduced method, which is distinct from overriding the inherited virtual
method.

The sibling COFF object-data classes in compiler/ogcoff.pas already declare
their Create(const n:string) constructors as overrides.  The FPC 2.0.2
compiler sources used by tp2cc have no TElf32ObjectData descendants and no
TElf32ObjectData class-reference construction path.  The object data is
created directly in TElf32ObjectOutput.NewObjectData by calling
TElf32ObjectData.Create(n).  Therefore changing this declaration from a
reintroduced method to an explicit override does not change an observed
bootstrap call path, while avoiding a same-signature reintroduced class
method that tp2cc cannot represent.

--- a/compiler/ogelf.pas
+++ b/compiler/ogelf.pas
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@ const
          plTSect,
          symsect  : telf32Section;
          syms     : Tdynamicarray;
-         constructor create(const n:string);
+         constructor create(const n:string);override;
          destructor  destroy;override;
          function  sectionname(atype:tasmsectiontype;const aname:string):string;override;
          procedure writereloc(data,len:aint;p:tasmsymbol;relative:TAsmRelocationType);override;
